        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1fecf733-6e0f-5158-9975-54949502c33d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan, China\n- Systems: Karakoram, Hispar Muztagh\n- Products: Trivor, The Crown, Huang Guan Shan, Crown Peak, Momhil Sar, Yengisogat\n\nFacts:\n- Trivor is a high peak of the Hispar Muztagh, which is a subrange of the Karakoram, in Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan.\n- The Crown is also known as Huang Guan Shan and sometimes Crown Peak, and it is a mountain in the Karakoram in China.\n- Momhil Sar is situated in the Hispar Muztagh subrange of the Karakoram a few kilometres northwest of its parent peak Trivor.\n- Yengisogat’s highest peak is Huangguan Shan, or Crown Peak, with a height of 7,265 m (23,835 ft), though it is also sometimes given as 7,295 m (23,934 ft).",
